# @COMMENT: This passage refers to the practice of Mālik b. Hubayrah, and his division of rows during funeral prayer. He is not mentioned in the redaction of Ibn Hishām. According to Ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam al-Miṣrī (d. 257/870), this is the only tradition attributed to Ibn Hubayrah (see, FMSXV01P344B). For reasons that are unclear, it is also one of the most widely circulated traditions in the Ibn Isḥāq corpus, both in terms of the number of witnesses, but in the distribution across the permodern literary tradtion. He was Mālik b. Hubayrah b. Khālid b. Muslim b. al-Ḥārith b. Bakr b. Thaʿlabah b. ʿAqabah b. sl-Sakrān, he was apparently a companion, although little is known about how or when you joined the community. He was sometimes listed as Mālik b. Hubayrah al-Sakūnī (see, for instance, QNMXV03P043A) and was close to Muʿāwiyah b. Abī Sifyān, who trusted his opinion and commanded armies for him. He died during the brief reign of Marwān (r. June 684-May 685), (see DKHXV05P289A). For its many witnesses and their variations, see: WYBWS: AZBNV01P292B, TMSXV03P338A , TDSHV56P509B, TDSHV56P510D, HKMXV02P530A; WSACD: TDSHV56P511A, TDSHV56P509B,  TDSHV56P510D, TDSHV56P512B, HKMXV02P530A, TMSXV03P338A; WHZZY: HBHXV27P281B, BKHBV07P303A, FMSXV01P344C, DWNXV03P202A, STBXV19P299A, BGHXV05P212B, QNMXV03P043B, NYMXV05P2467A, BQTMV06P329B, TDSHV56P509B, TDSHV56P509C, TDSHV56P511D, JWJXV07P030B, MZTXV27P166B; WMAAI: MHRXV02P503A, TDSHV56P509B, TDSHV56P510C; WHAYA: NSSXV01P516A, BQSXV04P048A, TDSHV56P509B, TDSHV56P511C; WABAB: HKMTV01P057A, NYMXV05P2467A; WISUL: NSSXV01P516A; WJHZA: NYMXV05P2467A, BQSXV04P048A, TDSHV56P509B, TDSHV56P510B, TDSHV56P511C; WAANH: TKXXV07P294E, SHMUV07P087A, SMJXV01P478A, DKHXV05P289A, NYMXV05P2467A; and WIBMK: FMSXV01P344B, TMSXV03P338A, HKMXV02P530A, NYMXV05P2467A, TDSHV56P509B, TDSHV56P510D. Its placement in the biographical section is based on content. EC_07/27/26@

